  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}}, \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}, \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}}$ are in A. P., then $\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}}\\right) \\left(\\frac{1}{b}+\\frac{1}{c}-\\frac{1}{a}\\right)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7HTnv",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{a c}-\\frac{3}{b^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "UW5nX",
      "text": "$\\frac{b^{2}-a c}{a^{2} b^{2} c^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CoEPh",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{a c}-\\frac{1}{b^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uCfr6",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{c}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$=\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{a}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{c}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}\\right)=\\frac{4}{\\mathrm{ac}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}}\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{a}}+\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{c}}\\right)+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{4}{\\mathrm{ac}}-\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{~b}}\\left(\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{~b}}\\right)+\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}=\\frac{4}{\\mathrm{ac}}-\\frac{3}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
